==Enemy==
This enemy occasionally fires off a devastating attack at extreme range in a very fast animation and has a lot of health with just one knockback. Fortunately, however, it's fairly slow for the threat it poses, and only really matters as a support unit when other, more dangerous threats enter play.

==Strategy==
Crazed Bird Cat's range is very high, effectively denying the use of units that inflict status effects and traditional backliners, but its attack frequency and DPS are rather low, with only 2.1k DPS. Adding on, this enemy's [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait can be easily exploited. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]] is the best example, who is able to rush in and secure lots of damage, but you could also damage Crazed Bird Cat with other melee units that are easily replaceable, such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cat]]/[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], since it has trouble stopping them from landing at least one hit. While units that outrange it are rare to come by, units such as a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] can help greatly in controlling its movement. Its low speed additionally makes it vulnerable to knockback effects, as well as [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]]. It is only troublesome when enemies like [[Bore]], [[Rain D.]] or [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe Cat]] appear, likely forcing you to deal with them while Crazed Bird Cat rains down fire unopposed.

